# Cases run with --profile max-sessions-1 in CI.
# The profile changes only the destination's sshd, so a case that never opens
# an SSH connection to destination runs exactly as in the default profile.
# List every case that contacts destination, directly or through a script it
# runs, and any case whose setup a listed case needs; leave out the others.
source build uploads itself over real SSH to empty helper caches
descriptor upload and download over real SSH
remote mapping generation
shared stream mappings over TCP and SSH
pipelined prune lookup with a one-deep data pipeline
ordinary SSH directory push and pull across separate hosts
restricted SSH worker handshake, revocation, and resume
long receiver home supports explicit SSH and blocked-TCP fallback
hardlinks survive SSH and TCP copies, updates, reruns, and pulls
# Sets up the return connection and receive root the next case uses.
named return destination works from independent server shells without agent forwarding
forward copies authorized through the return connection
restricted enrollment refuses an SSH control-plane destination
enrollment revocation stops active restricted receivers
source coordinator with constrained agent and restricted destination
comparison results and restricted receiver overwrite policies
expression selection on source, destination, and local coordinators
restricted expressions preserve container permissions and inheritance
destination firewall triggers automatic TCP fallback to SSH
source coordinator with constrained agent and SSH data channels
an unavailable direct SSH data route fails without relaying through the runner
destination coordinator with the reversed constrained-agent edge
local coordinator relaying between two SSH endpoints
tuning overrides for range uploads, downloads, direct copies, and relay
restricted authorization accepts 128 workers
adaptive worker ceilings through each remote coordinator
experimental streaming over TCP/SSH and each coordinator
batch overrides through a command-restricted receiver
